---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /karta/
title: Karta över gården
description: >-
  Karta över Stättareds 4H-gård med hagar, djurhus och allt annat på gården —
  och vilka djurslag som går var.
---
{#-
  The map page (02-§5.65). The map markup comes rendered from source/ts/build/map.ts;
  the list under it is the full text alternative (02-§5.24), in two groups so the places
  with animals come before the parking and the toilets (02-§5.51).
#}
<div class="container">
  <h1>Karta över gården</h1>

  {%- if views.map.html %}
  {{ views.map.html | safe }}
  {%- endif %}

  {%- for group in views.map.groups %}
  <section class="page-section">
    <h2>{{ group.heading }}</h2>
    <ul class="place-list">
      {%- for place in group.items %}
      <li class="place-list__item">
        <a class="place-list__link" href="{{ place.url | url }}">{{ place.symbol | safe }}{{ place.name }}</a>
        {%- if place.species %}
        <span class="place-list__species">{{ place.species }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}

  {#- Maps of the area belong to the main site and to Naturkartan, not here (02-§5.34,
      02-§1.8). Ordinary links: nothing is embedded and nothing is fetched (02-§5.26). #}
  <section class="page-section">
    <h2>Fler kartor i området</h2>
    <ul class="place-list">
      {%- for map in site.areaMaps %}
      <li class="place-list__item">
        <a class="place-list__link" href="{{ map.url }}">{{ map.name }}</a>
        <span class="place-list__note">{{ map.about }}</span>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>
